          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em inner automorphism 2-group
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            is essentially the sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AUT(G)
            of
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of those automorphisms that are connected by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfor"} transformation
            to the identity: this makes the automorphism necessarily an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+automorphism"} inner automorphism
          %p In fact, more precisely the inner automorphism 2-group is the 2-group of these connecting transformations, i.e. it remembers the group element and the inner automorphism that it induces under conjugation.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
          %p
            The
            %strong inner automorphism 2-group
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} INN(G)
            of
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                whose
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              .maruku-equation
                %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi Id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ⇓
                                %mi η
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                              %msub
                                %mo ↗
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp; \nearrow \searrow^{\mathrlap{Id}}
                      \\\
                      \\mathbf{B}G
                      \&amp;\Downarrow^{\eta}&amp;
                      \\mathbf{B}G
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \searrow \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\alpha}}
                      }
              %p
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            %li
              %p
                morphisms
                %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa : (\eta_1, \alpha_1) \to (\eta_2, \alpha_2)
                are commuting triangles of transformations
              .maruku-equation
                %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi Id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi η
                                      %mn 1
                              %mo ⇙
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ⇘
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi η
                                      %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⇒
                                %mi κ
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; Id
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\eta_1}}\swArrow &amp;&amp; \seArrow^{\mathrlap{\eta_2}}
                      \\\
                      \\alpha_1 &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\kappa}{\Rightarrow}&amp;&amp;
                      \\alpha_2
                      }
          %p
            Equivalently, this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ≕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  INN(G) = G//G \eqqcolon \mathbf{E}G
          %p
            of
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acting on itself.
          %p
            Equivalently , this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            corresponding to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Id
                    %mi G
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [INN(G)] =
                  \\left(
                  G \stackrel{Id}{\to} G
                  \\right)
          %p
            with action
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to Aut(G)
            given by right multiplication in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This makes it evident that
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} INN(G)
            is contractible
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B} INN(G) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} {*}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact, we may think of
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} INN(G)
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            in its incarnation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            (as opposed to the more tradition incarnation in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            theorem).
          %p To emphasize this we also write
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{E}G \coloneqq INN(G)
                  \\,.
          %p We have a natural sequence of groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \to \mathbf{E}G \to \mathbf{B}G
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is an old theorem by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
            that under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            followed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            this maps to the sequence of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \to \mathcal{E} G \to \mathcal{B}G
          %p
            that is the universal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            in its incarnation in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            The 2-group structure on
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} INN(G)
            is evident, and hence makes the fact evident that the universal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to \mathbf{E}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} deloops
            to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_1f60bf927b8aa3206977db63286a446bb6143c2e_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B} \mathbf{E}G
                  \\,.
          %p
            This fact is useful in various applications in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
